Z||000004||Loki||11-24-2001||11:02 PM||||Personally I dont like DSL..I thought it was slow, and some things it wouldnt stay connected....And of course you still have to "dial-up" in a sense..I like my cable ALOT!!! So far I maxed out on a d/l at 1200k/s...wasnt for like more than 10-15 seconds but the d/l was done   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and its "always-on"  But hey im not knocking it...I would take it if cable wasnt avaialble..Welcome to the high-speed internet fun   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||11-24-2001||11:29 PM||||DSL rocks! <BR>After waiting over a year for my phone company (BellSouth) to finally build out their infrastructure far enough out of town that I could get it, I finally got mine in April. Even kept my Mindspring e-mail address.<BR>You might want to invest in a router or some other means of insulation from the outside world. Not quite so important with DSL as with cable, but it's cheap insurance.||||reg||14
Z||000006||FormulaJoe||11-25-2001||10:05 AM||||Isnt high speed internet wonderfull?  Always hated to come home to dialup (had multiple T-1's at work, a university, tends to spoil you) have had cable for over a year now.  The router is a good idea to keep people out of your computer, even better if you have multiple computers sharing a connection(like me).  I dont know about DSL but my cable is always "on".  Started thinking the other day and started a channel on irc ( I seem to spend a lot of time there) on dal.net.  Call it Fieroclub (after I noticed several volvoclub channels) and since I have the always on connection am going to see if I can leave my client running 24/7 and see what happens.  If you online and doing irc..stop by and see if I am there.||||reg||6
